        "bbox": [
          107.0,
          459.0,
          888.0,
          783.0
        ],
        "source_type": "text",
        "source_sentence": "The effect of different tertiary amines on the $\\eta _ { \\mathrm { i n h } }$value of polymer IV were studied, the results showed that the $\\eta _ { \\mathrm { i n h } }$value of polymer IV was highest when tertiary amine was 2-methyl pyridine as the absorbent of HCl, because the basicity of N atom in -methyl pyridine was stronger than that in pyridine tributylamine, and triethylamine due to the electron donor effect (?I effect) of ortho-methyl group."
